# SHA-256 of every upstream file this SDK ships unmodified from the official
# FreeType 2.14.3 release.
#
#   https://download.savannah.gnu.org/releases/freetype/
#   released 2026-03-22  (docs/CHANGES:1, and the index listing's own date)
#   upstream VCS tag: VER-2-14-3  (ChangeLog:6)
#
# 854 records, 19676746 bytes: the 15 top-level files of the release plus
# include/ (102 files), src/ (451), builds/ (131), docs/ (146), tests/ (4),
# devel/ (2) and subprojects/ (3). That is the complete upstream file list in
# this tree, so a dependent receives the upstream project rather than a
# hand-picked subset of it. Nothing is dropped for size and nothing is dropped
# for being uncompiled by this fork: the four other build systems upstream
# ships, the HTML manuals, the historical release logs and the meson wrap
# files travel even though the Zig build reads only include/, src/ and
# builds/.
#
# ## The release tarball's own sha256 is NOT recorded, and this file does not
# ## invent one
#
# The canonical download index was read on 2026-10-05. It lists
# `freetype-2.14.3.tar.gz` (3.9 MiB) and `freetype-2.14.3.tar.xz` (2.5 MiB),
# both dated 2026-Mar-22 15:20, and beside each one only a detached `.sig`
# file. It publishes no checksum of either archive, so there is no digest to
# copy out of it. Which of the two archives this tree was imported from is also
# not recorded anywhere in this workspace, and no byte size below is the
# archive's: the numbers here are the sizes of the files in this tree.
#
# That gap is named rather than filled. A digest that was never observed would
# be a fabricated identifier in the one field whose purpose is to be
# unguessable, so the tarball digest is a prerequisite for the driver, which
# owns downloads: re-fetch the archive, compute its sha256, and add it to
# UPSTREAM.md and to this header in the same change. See FORK-NOTES.md.
#
# What *is* pinned here is the tree this SDK actually builds: every file below
# is digested, and tools/check-provenance.sh additionally rejects a missing,
# extra or renamed file under include/, src/, builds/, docs/, tests/, devel/
# and subprojects/, which a plain checksum run cannot see.
#
# ## tests/fixtures/ is not upstream and is not in this manifest
#
# The release's own `tests/` holds four files: README.md, meson.build,
# issue-1063/main.c and scripts/download-test-fonts.py, and the four records
# under tests/ above are exactly those. `tests/fixtures/` is this fork's
# directory: the vendored test font and its licence text, recorded as
# comments at the end of this file so that they are checked by
# tools/check-provenance.sh rather than by `sha256sum -c`.
#
# `sha256sum -c UPSTREAM.sha256` from the repository root checks the bytes.
